ction HomePage() {\n  return (\n    <main>\n      <h1>Hello world</h1>\n    </main>\n  );\n}\n```\nNotes for the applier: this is a server component (no `'use client'`), per the\n`component-composition` pattern in `docs/architecture/architecture.yaml`. The\n`<h1>` text must be exactly `Hello world` — `toHaveText` is an exact (trimmed)\nmatch, so do not add extra visible text inside the `h1`, and keep exactly one\n`h1` on the page so `page.locator('h1')` resolves to a single element.\n\n### Change #6: Container image used by docker-compose\n**File:** `services/frontend/Dockerfile`\n**Action:** Write (new file).\n**Content:**\n```dockerfile\nFROM node:20-alpine\n\nWORKDIR /app\n\nENV NEXT_TELEMETRY_DISABLED=1\nENV NODE_ENV=development\n\nCOPY package.json ./\nRUN npm install\n\nCOPY . .\n\nRUN npm run build\n\nENV NODE_ENV=production\nEXPOSE 3000\n\nCMD [\"npm\", \"run\", \"start\"]\n```\nNotes for the applier:\n- There is no lockfile, so `npm install` (not `npm ci`) is required.\n- `NODE_ENV=development` during install is deliberate: it keeps\n  `devDependencies` (typescript + @types) installed, which `next build` needs\n  to compile the `.tsx` sources; it is flipped back to `production` for runtime.\n- Do not switch the base image to a `-slim`/distroless variant or add a\n  multi-stage copy — keep it single-stage so `next start` finds `.next` and\n  `node_modules` in place.\n\n### Change #7: Keep host artifacts out of the build context\n**File:** `services/frontend/.dockerignore`\n**Action:** Write (new file).\n**Content:**\n```\nnode_modules\n.next\nnpm-debug.log\n.DS_Store\n```\n\n## Verification Expectations (do not run the test yourself)\nAfter the writes, the repo should contain `services/frontend/` with\n`package.json`, `next.config.mjs`, `tsconfig.json`, `Dockerfile`,\n`.dockerignore`, `app/layout.tsx`, and `app/page.tsx`. The compose build then\nsucceeds, the container serves `/` on container port 3000 bound to `0.0.0.0`,\nPlaywright's `webServer` URL probe 